hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16599","He said: Hajjaj and Hujayn narrated to us, they said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, from his uncle Abu Burdah, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, indeed we hastened a meat sheep of ours, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Before the prayer, I said: Yes, he said: That is a meat sheep, he said: O Messenger of Allah, indeed with us is a young jadhah goat, it is more beloved to me than an aged one, he said: It suffices for him, and it does not suffice for anyone after him."
"16600","He said: Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn Abdullah, from Abu Burdah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: None is flogged above ten lashes except in a hadd of the hudud of Allah Almighty."
"16601","He said: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr that Bukayr narrated to him, he said: While I was sitting with Sulayman ibn Yasar, Abd al-Rahman came narrating to Sulayman, then Sulayman turned to us and said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir narrated to me that his father narrated to him that he heard Abu Burdah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not flog more than ten lashes except in a hadd from the hudud of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Thus he said it to us in it. My father said: And I hold this view, meaning the hadith, meaning the hadith of Abu Burdah ibn Niyar."
"16602","He said: Surayj narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated to me that his father narrated to him that he heard Abu Burdah ibn Niyar al-Ansari saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not flog more than ten lashes except in a hadd from the hudud of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"16603","He said: Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Jumay or Abu Jumay, from his maternal uncle Abu Burdah ibn Niyar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw food and inserted his hand into it and saw something else, then said: He is not from us who deceives us."
"16604","He said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Bushayr ibn Yasar, mawla of Banu Harithah, narrated to me, from Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, he said: I witnessed the Eid with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: My wife went to my sacrificial animal when I left early for the prayer, and slaughtered it and prepared food from it. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer and I returned to her, she brought me food that had been finished. I said: Where is this from. She said: Your sacrifice; we slaughtered it and prepared food for you from it so you may eat lunch when you come. He said: I said to her: By Allah, I feared this may not be proper. He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: It is nothing; whoever slaughters before we finish our rite, it is nothing, so sacrifice. He said: I sought a musinnah and did not find it. He said: I came to him and said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I sought a musinnah and did not find it. He said: Seek a jadha from sheep and sacrifice it. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him the jadha from sheep, and he sacrificed it when he did not find the musinnah."
"16605","He said: Abdullah al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn Abdullah, from Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: None is flogged more than ten lashes in less than a hadd from the hudud of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Thus he said to us; he did not say: from his father."
